REQUIRES: z3
The constructs of a --smt2 query without a portable form are named in the
header (`; sea.smt2-nonportable <name>`) and warned
(smt2.nonportable.<name>), in both dialects.

A const-array (memory constants): z3 and Bitwuzla read it, Yices does not.
RUN: sea-vc %S/../bitwuzla/const-memory.mlir --program=join --lower --smt2 --smt2-dialect=portable > %t.c.smt2 2> %t.c.err
RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=CONST < %t.c.smt2
RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=CONSTWARN < %t.c.err
CONST: ; sea.smt2-dialect portable
CONST-NEXT: ; sea.smt2-nonportable const-array: read by z3 and Bitwuzla, not Yices; no portable form
CONST-NEXT: (set-logic ALL)
CONSTWARN: [smt2.nonportable.const-array]

z3's lambda (--mem=lambda without its simplifier): z3 only.
RUN: sea-vc %S/../memops/memmove-symbolic-overlap-above.mlir --program=unsat --lower --mem=lambda --lambda-simplify=none --smt2 > %t.l.smt2 2> %t.l.err
RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=LAMBDA < %t.l.smt2
RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=LAMBDAWARN < %t.l.err
LAMBDA: ; sea.smt2-dialect z3
LAMBDA-NEXT: ; sea.smt2-nonportable lambda: read by z3 only; no portable form
LAMBDA-NEXT: (set-logic ALL)
LAMBDAWARN: [smt2.nonportable.lambda]

The z3 dialect is the query z3 solves in-process, under --z3-logic's logic
too: it names the logic in a comment and declares ALL, so the z3 binary
reads it (under QF_BV it would reject the arrays and bvsmul_noovfl that
z3's API accepts).
RUN: sea-vc %S/../memops/memmove-symbolic-overlap-above.mlir --program=unsat --lower --z3-logic=QF_BV --smt2 > %t.za.smt2 2>/dev/null
RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=LOGIC < %t.za.smt2
RUN: %z3 %t.za.smt2 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=UNSAT
RUN: sea-vc %S/portable.mlir --program=smul_sat --z3-logic=QF_BV --smt2 > %t.zm.smt2 2>/dev/null
RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=LOGIC < %t.zm.smt2
RUN: %z3 %t.zm.smt2 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SAT
LOGIC: ; sea.z3-logic QF_BV
LOGIC-NEXT: (set-logic ALL)
UNSAT: {{^unsat$}}
SAT: {{^sat$}}

The portable dialect declares --z3-logic's logic; a query outside it is
warned.
RUN: sea-vc %S/../memops/memmove-symbolic-overlap-above.mlir --program=unsat --lower --z3-logic=QF_BV --smt2 --smt2-dialect=portable > %t.pa.smt2 2> %t.pa.err
RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=PLOGIC < %t.pa.smt2
RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=PLOGICWARN < %t.pa.err
PLOGIC: ; sea.smt2-logic-mismatch arrays outside QF_BV
PLOGIC-NEXT: (set-logic QF_BV)
PLOGICWARN: [smt2.logic-mismatch]

The dialect is z3's printer's: not with another solver.
RUN: %if yices %{ not sea-vc %S/../memops/memmove-symbolic-overlap-above.mlir --solver=yices --smt2 --smt2-dialect=portable 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SOLVER %}
SOLVER: --smt2-dialect needs --solver=z3

